📄 Default Username in the Service File
The default username set in your wro_robot.service file is:

text
User=pi
📂 Exact Line from Your Service File
ini
[Service]
Type=simple
User=pi
WorkingDirectory=/home/pi/wro_future_engineers_2026
ExecStart=/home/pi/wro_future_engineers_2026/venv/bin/python3 /home/pi/wro_future_engineers_2026/main.py
⚠️ Important – What This Means for You
Scenario	What You Must Do
You create a user named pi	✅ Everything works as-is – no changes needed.
You create a user with a different name (e.g., teamobsidian)	❌ The service will fail because the user pi doesn't exist. You must edit wro_robot.service and change User=pi to User=teamobsidian. Also update the paths from /home/pi/... to /home/teamobsidian/....
🔧 How to Fix If You Choose a Different Username
Edit the service file before running the installer:

bash
nano scripts/wro_robot.service
Change:

ini
User=teamobsidian
WorkingDirectory=/home/teamobsidian/wro_future_engineers_2026
ExecStart=/home/teamobsidian/wro_future_engineers_2026/venv/bin/python3 /home/teamobsidian/wro_future_engineers_2026/main.py
Then run the installer as usual.

✅ Recommendation
To avoid extra steps, use pi as your username when installing Raspberry Pi OS. That way, everything works without any modifications. 🚀

